ithub.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Part 1, just getting several things out of the way so we can discuss sooner.\n\nThere's a lot of improvements here and it's overall very welcome. The audio-related class reference has been smelling old and lacking in details.\n\nAs I understand, the PR isn't meant to standardize this side of the class reference, but given that it affects so much at once, it should be expected.\nYet, there are a lot of minor inconsistencies across multiple affected descriptions which add up. To be clear, what bothers me personally is that the affected descriptions add **more** inconsistency, instead of at least keeping the current state of things.\n\nThere's also a lot of cases where \"_this audio stream_\" was changed to \"_the stream_\" and I am frankly not sure why, other than preference.\n\n> Maybe closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115825\n\nJust a tip. GitHub detects specific keywords (like \"_closes_\") behind issue links in the PR's description, and automatically closes them when the PR is merged. If you're very in doubt, do not use those keywords, otherwise we may need to manually reopen it.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119334#pullrequestreview-4352536310","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengi